    content: 'Baldur\'s Gate 3 Honour Mode, introduced with Patch 5, is the definitive hardcore D&D experience. In Honour Mode, you have only 1 life (permadeath), all enemies gain +20% HP and +2 to all saving throws, and Legendary Actions are added to boss fights (e.g., Myrkul can use \'Command: Grovel\' as a legendary action). This guide covers the 12 hardest encounters in Honour Mode: 1. Paladins of Tyr (Act1, 4 Paladins, 200 HP each). 2. Grym (Act1, forge boss, 300 HP, immune to fire). 3. Auntie Ethel (Act1, 150 HP, 3 duplicates). 4. Gerringothe Thorm (Act2, 400 HP, regenerates 20 HP/sec). 5. Thisobald Thorm (Act2, 350 HP, 5 beer-themed attacks). 6. Myrkul, Lord of Bones (Act2, 500 HP, Legendary Action: Command). 7. Orin the Red (Act3, 450 HP, shapeshifts into party member). 8. Gortash (Act3, 400 HP, 5 steel watchers). 9. Raphael (Act3, 600 HP, 6 cambions). 10. The Netherbrain (Act3, 800 HP, 3 mind flayers). The best party composition: 1. Tav (Oathbreaker Paladin 5 / Thief Rogue 4 / Champion Fighter 3, 2-handed greatsword). 2. Shadowheart (Life Cleric 12, mass healing). 3. Astarion (Thief Rogue 4 / Champion Fighter 8, ranged DPS). 4. Gale (Evocation Wizard 12, AoE control). Estimated completion time: 80-120 hours. Difficulty: 9/10. Reward: Golden Dice (cosmetic, all dice rolls show gold).',
    coverImage: 'https://cdn.cloudflare.steamstatic.com/steam/apps/1245620/header.jpg',
    gameId: 'baldurs-gate-3',
